  "query_preview": "until late Wed morning and I also added northern Blaine\nCounty to the winter weather advisory. \n\nOverall, light rain/snow continues to move northward through the\nCWA. A few pockets of moderate snowfall (visibility around 1/2\nmile) have occurred for a short time. The rain is changing to \nsnow at most lower elevations this evening. It will likely take \nuntil late evening for the rain to change to snow in the \nHavre/Harlem areas. Some areas have had close to 0.30 inches of \nrainfall already (Bozeman)...with areas near Bynum reporting near \n3 inches of snowfall.\n\nThe snow will generally end for west to east on Wednesday, ending\nin the west Wed morning and in the east Wed afternoon. \nTemperatures look on track. Brusda",
